{"user": "why is the a8 corner usually dangerous?", "user_ts": "2026-08-07T12:42:05.152485+00:00", "assistant": "The **a8 corner itself is not dangerous** \u2014 corners are great because once you own them, they can\u2019t be flipped.\n\nWhat\u2019s usually dangerous are the squares **next to an empty corner**:\n\n- **a7** and **b8** touch a8 directly  \n- **b7** is the diagonal \u201cX-square\u201d next to a8\n\nPlaying one of those can give White a way to play **a8 next**, which would make White\u2019s corner permanent and often stabilize the whole left/bottom edge.\n\nIn endgames, though, this rule can have exceptions because mobility and final disc count may matter more.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-07T12:42:15.468813+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-07T12:42:17.119512+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Hint": 2}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Hint": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Board Report": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Board Report":